From a6666f5a4f0172a79ff09c1b7902104af0dbd7df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeevaka Prabu Badrappan <jeevaka.badrappan@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Aug 2024 14:58:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] gralloc/imapper5: Changes to use IMapper5 stable-c
 mapper

As IMapper4 is deprecated from Android15, changes done to use
IMapper5 stable-c mapper.

Tests done:
- Android boot in GVT-d and BM config
- adb reboot

Adapted for Mesa 26.0.3 (A17 review):
 - IMapper4 stays available for every SDK >= 30. The stable-C IMapper5
   backend (u_gralloc_imapper5_api_create) is tried first and IMapper4
   is the fallback, so devices upgraded to Android 15+ that keep an
   IMapper4 mapper still get a metadata backend. dep_android_mapper5 is
   attached to u_gralloc and exported like dep_android_mapper4.
 - The mapper library, the AIMapper_loadIMapper lookup and the mapper
   are resolved once in one cached scope (NULL on failure), so a broken
   library falls back cleanly and no closed handle is ever reused.
 - importBuffer gets the native handle directly; the requested format
   is read from the already imported handle.
 - Plane layouts are bounded by the output arrays. The YUV FourCC is
   rebuilt from the chroma plane only when it describes Cb/Cr and the
   derived format has the same plane count; otherwise the mapper FourCC
   is kept. For semi-planar chroma the Cb/Cr order comes from the
   components' bit offsets, not from their order in the list.
 - Colour info is always fully initialised, and ChromaSiting
   COSITED_VERTICAL/COSITED_BOTH are handled as upstream does.

Tracked-On: OAM-122192
Signed-off-by: Jeevaka Prabu Badrappan <jeevaka.badrappan@intel.com>
(cherry picked from commit a9a5aaf031f1e84206cd6b6a0c8c0a67b5da5a51)
Tracked-On: NIACP3-1589
Signed-off-by: Basanagouda Nagappa Koppad <basanagouda.nagappa.koppad@intel.com>
